  m_text: 'Every component in the course keeps the same order, marked by comment lines: Variables (public), Variables (private), Events, Unity Lifecycle, Actions, Gizmos. A script has only the sections it uses. Unity does not need this order; it makes every script read the same way. The Inspector shows the same groups: Public, Private (read-only), Events.


    <b>Predict:</b> Which of the six sections does Blinker not have?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Press Play. Select Lamp 5 and open Code Watch.

    2. Match the section lines of Blinker with the groups in the Inspector.

    3. Click Call beside StopBlinking, then beside StartBlinking.'
