  m_text: 'A class is a template. Each time Spinner is added to a GameObject, Unity makes a new component from the same template, with its own values. The three cubes carry one file, Spinner.cs, but each component has its own degreesPerSecond and its own angle.


    <b>Predict:</b> You set Degrees Per Second to 0 on Cube 3B. What do Cube 3A and Cube 3C do?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Press Play. Select each cube in turn and read the values of its Spinner.

    2. On Cube 3B, set Degrees Per Second to 0.

    3. Find 90f in Spinner.cs: the value a new Spinner starts with.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
